# Falls back to React Native core's classic fetch/XMLHttpRequest instead of
# this Expo SDK's own WinterCG-compliant fetch (installed by default as of
# this SDK version — see node_modules/expo/src/winter/runtime.native.ts).
#
# Not a secret — EXPO_PUBLIC_ vars are inlined into the client bundle by
# design, safe to commit and share across the team.
#
# Why: found three separate bugs in the newer fetch/expo-file-system native
# bridge layer while building PDF import's file upload (see git history on
# src/lib/ai.ts for the full trace of each): a FormData-part interop shim
# that doesn't recognize RN's own {uri,name,type} file shape, an
# expo-file-system UploadTaskOptions field-order mismatch, and (this one)
# custom headers beyond content-type apparently not surviving the trip
# through the newer fetch's native request layer. RN's classic fetch (this
# flag) routes through NetworkingModule.kt instead, which was independently
# confirmed correct for all of the above while tracing bug #1. Revisit this
# flag if a future SDK bump fixes the underlying issues upstream — it's a
# blanket workaround, not something to leave forever without reason.
EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_RN_FETCH=1
